// REJECTS: Unexpected token '/'. Valid alternatives: ['Class', 'Association', 'Profile'
//
// A `/*` never closed. The lexer does not run the comment to end-of-input and quietly
// swallow the file: the unterminated comment fails to match the comment rule at all, so
// '/' arrives at the parser as a token in element position.
//
// This is a documented past defect of this very harness, in the other direction -- a '//'
// inside a string literal was once stripped as a comment and ate the rest of the file. The
// failure mode a rewrite risks here is the mirror: treating an unterminated /* as
// "comment to EOF" makes this file parse as EMPTY, which is not an error, produces no
// elements, and reports success on a file whose entire content was discarded.
###Pure
/* this comment is never closed
Class fixture::neg::AfterComment
{
   code: String[1];
}
